<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             x:Class="TanMenu.Wpf.Views.Settings.AboutCard"
             FontSize="{DynamicResource FontSizeBody}">
  <!-- ══ 关于 — the whole content of the About box ═══════════════════════════════════════════
       WHERE THIS CARD LIVES. It is the entire content of Dialogs/AboutWindow.axaml, a modal About
       box the menu band's 关于 item opens. PUBLISHED, win-property-win: "Is the content solely an
       application's attributes? If so, use an About box." It is: this is the only settings group
       with no interactive control at all, which is the same fact that used to justify its position
       and now justifies its surface. (Round 5, item 2 — "关于集成到设置页中" — had folded it INTO the
       settings surface as the last group of the 设置 page; Round 8, Task 2 turned that page into a
       tabbed dialog and this card became its sixth tab; Task 4 took the tab out into a window.)

       ── ROUND 8, TASK 6 DELETED THE GROUP BOX, AND WITH IT THE DOUBLED 关于 ────────────────────
       Task 4 left the box exactly as the tab had it and said so in AboutWindow.axaml's own prose,
       because re-cutting the card there would have put that task's markup and this one's in conflict
       over one file. The cost, visible in Task 4's own capture, was that the word 关于 appeared
       TWICE on a window whose whole content is four lines: once as the window's title (written by
       AboutWindow.ApplyText from AppLanguage's "About") and once as the box's own header, written
       from the very same key. A group box round the only group on a surface is what
       ctrl-group-boxes says to indicate on the larger surface instead — "Are all the controls inside
       the group? If so, indicate the relationship on the larger surface, such as the parent dialog
       box or page" — and here that surface is a window with a caption. The header TextBlock and its
       ReloadFromConfig assignment are both gone.

       THE 11 AT THE BOTTOM IS NOT DECORATION. The deleted box carried Margin="0,0,0,11" from
       Themes/Shell/Launcher.axaml's HeaderedContentControl.tm-group-box, and AboutWindow's button
       row deliberately states NO top margin because that 11 was already inside this card's desired
       size (its own prose and AboutWindowTests both record the arithmetic). Deleting the box without
       restating the 11 here would have put 确定 hard against the copyright line. 11 is PUBLISHED,
       vis-layout: "Between unrelated controls — 7 / 11".

       THE FontSize ON THIS ROOT IS THE SAME ONE THE OTHER FIVE CARDS STATE, and this card needs it
       for the same reason and one extra: deleting the group box above also deleted the last thing
       on this window that set a FontSize at all. AboutWindow is an Avalonia Window, so FluentTheme's
       {x:Type Window} ControlTheme gives it ControlContentThemeFontSize = 14, and every one of the
       four lines below is a bare TextBlock. AppearanceCard.axaml's header carries the whole
       mechanism and the measurements.

       THE ICON. The 16 DIP product tile rather than a Segoe glyph — this content is the app itself,
       and the image is already compiled into the assembly for SplashPanel and for the Aero caption's
       own icon (MainWindow.axaml's WindowDecorationsTheme). Width AND Height are stated here because
       the :is(Control).tm-card-icon class that used to set the width went with the row grammar, and
       an Image has no line box to supply a height. 7 to the text is PUBLISHED, "Between related
       controls — 4 / 7": a mark and the label it marks are related.

       THE TITLE IS A XAML LITERAL, and the one label anywhere on the settings surface that is not
       localized: "TanMenu" is the product's name, identical in both languages. The publisher line
       below it IS localized (AppLanguage's AboutPublisher).

       NEITHER VALUE LINE SETS A ToolTip, and that is deliberate rather than an omission. A value
       line whose text can outgrow the surface it sits on and has no ToolTip is a defect; neither of
       these can, because both are fixed formats over fixed content, not user data — and the window
       they sit on is SizeToContent, so it is as wide as the widest of them BY CONSTRUCTION. It is
       the same reasoning FoldersCard's DataInfoText records, and the opposite of its two path lines,
       which are user data and do set one. -->
  <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="7" Margin="0,0,0,11">
    <Image Grid.Column="0" Width="16" Height="16" VerticalAlignment="Top"
           Source="avares://TanMenu.Wpf/wwwroot/app-tile.png" />
    <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" Spacing="3">
      <TextBlock Text="TanMenu" />
      <TextBlock x:Name="PublisherText" />
      <TextBlock x:Name="VersionLine" />
      <TextBlock x:Name="CopyrightLine" />
    </StackPanel>
  </Grid>
</UserControl>
